<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Pokémon Summary Preview</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0;background:#14161c;color:#dde;font:13px system-ui,sans-serif;padding:16px;max-width:1000px;margin-inline:auto}
h1{font-size:20px;margin:0 0 4px}.sub{color:#8a93a6;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:12px}
#stage{background:#0a0b10;border:1px solid #2c3140;border-radius:10px;display:flex;justify-content:center;padding:10px;line-height:0}
#scr{image-rendering:pixelated;width:720px;max-width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:3/2;outline:none;cursor:pointer;background:#000}
.row{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin:10px 0}
button,select,input,textarea{font:inherit;background:#262a36;color:#eef;border:1px solid #3a4052;border-radius:6px;padding:7px 11px}
button{cursor:pointer}button:hover{background:#343b50}button.pri{background:#3a6df0;border-color:#5d8aff}button.ok{background:#2e8b57;border-color:#3fb37a}
label.in{display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center;color:#9ab}
code{background:#262a36;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px;color:#cfe}
section{background:#1c1f28;border:1px solid #2c3140;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;margin-top:14px}
h2{font-size:14px;margin:0 0 6px;color:#7fa4ff}
.hint{color:#8a93a6;line-height:1.5}
textarea{width:100%;height:240px;font:12px/1.4 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;white-space:pre;overflow:auto}
#status{color:#9ab;line-height:1.6;margin-top:6px}.good{color:#6fe3a0}.warn{color:#ffd166}
.keys{color:#8a93a6;margin-top:8px;line-height:1.7}.keys b{color:#cfe;font-weight:600}
#msg{background:#222a40;border:1px solid #3a6df0;border-radius:8px;padding:8px 12px;margin-top:10px;display:none}
input[type=number]{width:64px}
</style></head><body>
<h1>Pokémon Summary Screen</h1>
<div class="sub">GBA size (240×160) party menu and summary screens, drawn with your own sprites, icons and the Emerald font. Everything is animated and runs in the browser. Save a PNG at <b>2×</b> to get exactly the 480×320 top screen of your game.</div>

<div id="stage"><canvas id="scr" width="240" height="160" tabindex="0"></canvas></div>
<div class="keys"><b>Arrows / W S A D</b> move · <b>Z / Enter</b> = A (open, select) · <b>X / Esc</b> = B (back) · <b>Q / E</b> or <b>← →</b> change page · <b>↑ ↓</b> change Pokémon · click a row to select, click it again to open</div>

<div class="row">
  <button class="pri" id="bFolder">Choose project folder</button>
  <button id="bDb">PokemonDatabase.js</button>
  <button id="bTT">TypeTables.js</button>
  <button id="bSave">save.json</button>
  <label class="in">Frames in a sprite sheet
    <select id="frames"><option value="auto">auto (wide sheet = 4)</option><option value="1">1</option><option value="2">2</option><option value="4">4</option></select></label>
  <label class="in"><input type="checkbox" id="shiny"> shiny frame</label>
  <label class="in"><input type="checkbox" id="cries"> cries</label>
  <label class="in">text nudge Y <input type="number" id="nudge" value="0" min="-4" max="4"></label>
  <input type="file" id="fFolder" webkitdirectory multiple hidden><input type="file" id="fDb" accept=".js,.txt" hidden><input type="file" id="fTT" accept=".js,.txt" hidden><input type="file" id="fSave" accept=".json,.txt" hidden>
</div>
<div class="row">
  <button id="bHurt">Hurt −12 HP</button><button id="bHeal">Heal +12 HP</button>
  <label class="in"><input type="checkbox" id="demo"> auto demo</label>
  <label class="in">export size <select id="scale"><option value="1">1× (240×160)</option><option value="2" selected>2× (480×320)</option><option value="3">3× (720×480)</option><option value="4">4× (960×640)</option></select></label>
  <button class="ok" id="bPng">Save this screen (PNG)</button>
  <button class="ok" id="bSheet">Save all 4 screens (PNG)</button>
  <button class="ok" id="bRec">Record 14 s video</button>
</div>
<div id="msg"></div>
<div id="status"></div>

<section>
  <h2>This page runs the real game module</h2>
  <div class="hint">The screen above is drawn by <code>js/PokemonSummary.js</code> itself (it is built into this page), so what you see here is what the game shows when the player presses Enter.
    Press <b>Choose project folder</b> and pick the folder that holds <code>graphics/</code>, <code>audio/</code> and <code>tables/</code>: the page picks up the sprites, icons, font, cries,
    <code>PokemonDatabase.js</code> and <code>TypeTables.js</code> by file name. Nothing is uploaded, it is only read in your browser.</div>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>Party (save format)</h2>
  <div class="hint">Same shape as <code>GameStateManager.saveData.party</code> / <code>save.json</code>: a list of Pokémon (a whole save with a <code>party</code> in it works too). In the game the party comes from the live save, here you can paste your own and press Apply, or load a <code>save.json</code>.</div>
  <textarea id="partyTxt" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
  <div class="row"><button class="pri" id="bApply">Apply party</button></div>
</section>

